# Cloudflare Pages applies these headers to static assets. Every rule that
# matches is applied, so the site-wide block below stands for everything and the
# per-directory blocks only add caching on top of it.

# Allow the app to be embedded as a Discord Activity (iframe under
# discord.com / discordsays.com).
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors https://discord.com https://*.discord.com https://*.discordsays.com

# Caching, per directory.
#
# Pages' default is `max-age=0, must-revalidate`: right for `index.html`, wrong
# for the board models, because the homepage mounts the real renderer and a
# first visit pulls the models before an island appears. The hero recording
# draws 13 files and the landing warm-up asks for the base ruleset's 17; as
# shipped (meshopt, `npm run models:compress`) those are 809 KB and 967 KB, and
# all 37 are 1,692 KB. The counts drift: recount with
# `find frontend/public/models -name '*.glb'` and `boardModelFiles("base")` in
# lib/board3d/loader.ts.
#
# That is also the difference somebody reported as "the map only loads when I am
# logged in": a logged-in player has played, so their browser holds the models
# and revalidation is a handful of 304s. Nobody else has them.

# THE HTML, SPELLED OUT RATHER THAN INHERITED.
#
# This is Pages' own default (`public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`), so it
# changes nothing today. It is written down because it is the one cache decision
# in this file that would be most damaging to get wrong, and an unstated default
# reads exactly like an oversight: index.html names the content-hashed entry
# chunk, so a cached copy pins the visitor to the build it was cached from. That
# failure is quiet -- every /assets/* URL the stale HTML names is immutable and
# still resolvable, so nothing 404s and nothing looks broken; they just run an
# old app until the copy expires.
#
# Two exact paths, not a wildcard, because these rules match the REQUEST path.
# `/` and `/index.html` are the two ways to ask for it directly. Every other SPA
# route (/play, /game/<id>, ...) is served the same bytes through the _redirects
# catch-all and matches neither, so it takes the same Pages default by
# inheritance, which is the answer we want. A wildcard broad enough to catch
# those routes would also catch /assets/*, and the rule below is the one thing
# here that must not be weakened.
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Vite's own output, content-hashed by the build. A new build is a new filename,
# so these can be cached as hard as the header allows.
#
# `immutable` here is why /assets/* goes through the Pages Function: these
# headers are matched on the request path, so a miss that the _redirects
# catch-all turned into index.html would be pinned as a year-long, immutable
# lump of HTML at a JavaScript URL. functions/_middleware.js turns that miss back
# into a no-store 404 before it can be cached.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Not content-hashed: `pieces.glb` has the same name in every build, so a year
# would keep new art from anyone who had the old. A day fresh, then a week of
# stale-while-revalidate. `immutable` would need hashed names, which means
# teaching `make export-assets`, `manifest.generated.ts` and loader.ts's
# COMMON_MODELS/KNIGHTS_MODELS about the hash; not worth it for a return visit
# that is already instant.
#
# cf-cache-status: DYNAMIC cannot be fixed from this file. Cloudflare decides
# cache eligibility from the file extension before reading Cache-Control, and
# `.glb` is not in its default set (changing Content-Type does not help). The
# same check is why these are served with no content-encoding.
#
# The fix is a dashboard change on the zone, and it has to be made by hand:
#   Cloudflare dashboard, costan.io, Caching, Cache Rules, Create rule
#     - When incoming requests match: URI Path starts with /models/
#     - Cache eligibility: Eligible for cache
#     - Edge TTL: Use cache-control header from origin
#   and, on the same screen's sibling (Rules, Compression Rules), a rule for the
#   same path with Brotli enabled if the plan offers it.
# Meshopt-compressed .glb is already entropy-coded, so the compression rule is
# worth a few percent; the cache rule is the one that matters, and it turns a
# first visit from an origin fetch into an edge hit.
/models/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/cosmetics/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

# Subset and stable: the file only changes when the character set does, which is
# a deliberate act (scripts/gen-title-fonts.py) and rare.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000, stale-while-revalidate=604800
